    STAS-299: stamp the stranded hold-lane card failed when self-heal fails its gate row
    
    FN-8492's sweep rewrote a dead pending step result to failed and stopped. On a
    plan-in-place board the card stayed in its hold lane with status:null: the graph
    will not re-dispatch a failed gate, the scheduler does not re-plan a card whose
    gate row exists, and every retry surface admits only a card-level failure - so a
    dead review session left the card with no recovery owner (STAS-281, 2.2 days).
    
    Failure on this board is a status, not a lane (COLUMNS and VALID_TRANSITIONS
    declare no failed entry), so ownership is status+error written in the same patch,
    with no move, scoped to the trait-resolved hold-lane set and only when the card
    carries no status yet.

