    STAS-299: name the stranded-gate retry class once, in core
    
    Every retry surface re-derived its own idea of what is retryable, so an agent's fn_task_retry, the
    CLI, the chat tool and the board's Retry button could answer one card four ways — the
    FNXC:WorkflowLifecycleColumns defect class. The board's answer for this shape was also the worst
    available: the locked stage restart serves a hold-lane card with scope "plan", which stamps
    needs-replan, empties the step list, clears the approved-plan fingerprint and force-deletes
    PROMPT.md — and needs-replan refuses every release mode, so the retry would have traded one dead
    zone for a permanent one.
    
    classifyStrandedGateRetry + buildStrandedGateRetryPatch are now the single classification and patch:
    pre-execution (hold/intake) lane by trait role, an approved plan still on the card, and failure
    evidence that is only a required pre-merge gate row which failed without ever carrying a verdict
    (RUFU-217's class, so a re-run overturns no reviewer authority). The patch re-queues through the
    shipped manual-retry reset, clears the failure state, and discharges exactly those verdict-less gate
    rows — the same row-level discard a column restart already does, narrowed — while leaving lane,
    steps, currentStep, fingerprint, PROMPT.md and the checkout untouched.

