CommitDate: Tue Oct 13 03:44:14 2026 +0200

    retry: one verdict-less gate answer on the board, the CLI, the extension and chat
    
    STAS-299 req 4 + Invariant C. A card self-heal stranded in a hold lane — an approved plan whose
    required Plan/Code Review row was flipped to `failed` with no verdict while the card itself carries
    no status — was retryable on NO surface: each one admitted only a card-level `failed` /
    `stuck-killed`, or an in-review stall. Where a surface did answer, its answer was destructive: the
    dashboard asked the locked stage planner, which serves a hold-lane card with `scope: "plan"` and
    answers `needs-replan` + emptied `steps` + cleared `approvedPlanFingerprint` + deleted PROMPT.md,
    and `fn task retry`'s generic fallthrough clears `worktree`, `branch`, `baseBranch` and
    `baseCommitSha`. Both trade away the work for a verdict that never arrived — and `needs-replan` is
    refused by every release mode, so the dashboard Retry converted a recoverable dead zone into a
    permanent one.
    
    Each surface now classifies the card against the workflow IR it already resolved and, for this one
    class, applies core's shared patch: clear the failure state, drop only the verdict-less gate rows so
    the graph's own gate re-evaluates as `missing`, touch nothing else. The card does NOT move — a hold
    lane is where it already sits, and RUFU-261 exists because a user-sourced move into a hold lane can
    park the card a retry was asked to run. The branch sits first after the recovery-budget reset, so no
    later branch can run for this shape; the classification excludes review lanes, so no existing
    branch's shape changes and a genuine planning/replan card keeps the destructive restart.
    
    Also tightens `buildStoreBootStallResult`'s declared `details`: Step 3's `Record<string, unknown>`
    erased the `error` member the extension tool wrapper's error branch requires, which is a latent
    compile error in packages/cli that only a full `tsc -p` shows. Surfaced while typechecking here.
    
    Verified: tsc clean for core/engine/dashboard/cli; cli `task-retry`, `task-retry-renamed-review`
    (PG), `extension-store-boot-transience` and `extension-agent-class-boot-budget` suites green.

